    "narrative": "For August 25, the Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Vinnie Pasquantino**, whose score of 76.21 makes him our highest-projected asset today. He benefits from a prime matchup against Scherzer, whose 5.31 xERA provides the most favorable SP context on our board, augmented by a massive +14% platoon boost. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start at 74.41; despite facing Holmes, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite sprint speed profile thrives even against tougher arms, and his placement in the #2 spot provides enough volume to overcome the slight negative drag from the opponent's 53% SB hold rate. **Isaac Paredes** and **Seiya Suzuki** also project as \"Strong\" plays, with **Isaac Paredes** buoyed by a +9% platoon edge and **Seiya Suzuki** benefiting from a high-frequency SB opportunity against a slower delivery.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Austin Riley**, who finished with a 42.81 efficiency score. While **Austin Riley** has the pedigree to perform, he was squeezed out of the utility and corner slots by the superior matchup data favoring **Vinnie Pasquantino** and our infield starters. The optimizer favored the floor of our starters over **Austin Riley**'s ceiling against Glasnow, who carries a significantly tougher 3.01 xERA. Elsewhere, we are monitoring **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom present elevated risk. **Jose Caballero** is hindered by a brutal -13% platoon adjustment and a bottom-of-the-order assignment, while **Mickey Moniak** faces a challenging platoon disadvantage (-15%) against Alvarez. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Henry Bolte** at the top of the lineup to capitalize on his +10% park factor to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories.",
